  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1015 PM CST Tue Nov 17 2026\n\nThe strong area of high pressure will be pushing off to the\nnortheast on Friday as long wave troughing starts to lift out of \nthe Western US. This will bring some changes to our weather \npattern but overall won't bring much in the way of rain chances. A\nshort wave and increase in moisture will bring a low chance for\nshowers on Saturday (10%) but will mainly bring increased cloud \ncover. A surface low and trough pushing through the Great Lakes \nwill push a cold front east into Middle TN on Sunday. This will \nbring higher rain chances (20-30%) during the afternoon and \nevening but overall those look to stay on the low side. CAPE will \nbe minimal ahead of the cold front keeping the thunderstorm threat\nvery low. Strong Canadian high pressure will quickly build in \nover the central part of the country early next week bringing the \nreturn of quiet and cooler weather. Highs Friday and into the \nweekend will be mild in the mid 60s to lower 70s but will cool \nback into the 50s behind the cold front.",
